#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/quick-help.mdx
msgid "<b>Zero Page</b> (<tt>$c0</tt>): Access memory locations <tt>$00</tt>-<tt>$FF</tt>"
msgstr "<b>Pagina zero</b> (<tt>$c0</tt>): Acceder locationes de memoria <tt>$00</tt>-<tt>$FF</tt>"

#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/quick-help.mdx
msgid "<b>Zero Page</b>: <tt>$0000</tt>-<tt>$00FF</tt> (first 256 bytes, faster access)"
msgstr "<b>Pagina zero</b>: <tt>$0000</tt>-<tt>$00FF</tt> (prime 256 bytes, accesso plus rapide)"

#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/tutorial.mdx
msgid "<tt>BCC</tt> and <tt>BCS</tt> (\"branch on carry clear\" and \"branch on carry set\") are used to branch on the carry flag. Write a program that uses one of these two."
msgstr "<tt>BCC</tt> e <tt>BCS</tt> (\"ramificar sur reporto clar\" e \"ramificar sur reporto definite\") es usate pro ramificar sur le bandiera de reporto. Scribe un programma que usa un de iste duo."

#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/tutorial.mdx
msgid "<tt>JMP</tt> is an unconditional jump. Here's a really simple example to show it in action:"
msgstr "<tt>JMP</tt> es un salto inconditional. Ecce un exemplo realmente simple pro monstrar lo in action:"

#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/tutorial.mdx
msgid "<tt>JSR</tt> and <tt>RTS</tt> (\"jump to subroutine\" and \"return from subroutine\") are a dynamic duo that you'll usually see used together. <tt>JSR</tt> is used to jump from the current location to another part of the code. <tt>RTS</tt> returns to the previous position. This is basically like calling a function and returning."
msgstr "<tt>JSR</tt> e <tt>RTS</tt> (\"saltar a subrutina\" e \"retornar de subrutina\") es un duo dynamic que tu usualmente vide usate insimul. <tt>JSR</tt> es usate pro saltar del location currente a un altere parte del codice. <tt>RTS</tt> retorna al position previe. Isto es basicamente como appellar un function e retornar."

#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/tutorial.mdx
msgid "<tt>PC</tt> is the program counter - it's how the processor knows at what point in the program it currently is. It's like the current line number of an executing script. In the simulator the code is assembled starting at memory location <tt>$0600</tt>, so <tt>PC</tt> always starts there."
msgstr "<tt>PC</tt> es le contator de programma - es como le processor sape a qual puncto in le programma illo currentemente es. Es como le numero de linea currente de un script executante. In le simulator le codice es assemblate comenciante a location de memoria <tt>$0600</tt>, assi <tt>PC</tt> sempre comencia ibi."

#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/tutorial.mdx
msgid "<tt>SP</tt> is the stack pointer. I won't get into the stack yet, but basically this register is decremented every time a byte is pushed onto the stack, and incremented when a byte is popped off the stack."
msgstr "<tt>SP</tt> es le punctator de pila. Io non entrara in le pila ancora, ma basicamente iste registro es decrementate cata vice que un byte es pushate sur le pila, e incrementate quando un byte es poppate del pila."

#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/tutorial.mdx
msgid "<tt>X</tt> holds the pixel colour, and <tt>Y</tt> holds the position of the current pixel. The first loop draws the current colour as a pixel (via the <tt>A</tt> register), pushes the colour to the stack, then increments the colour and position. The second loop pops the stack, draws the popped colour as a pixel, then increments the position. As should be expected, this creates a mirrored pattern."
msgstr "<tt>X</tt> mantene le color del pixel, e <tt>Y</tt> mantene le position del pixel currente. Le prime loop designa le color currente como pixel (per le registro <tt>A</tt>), pusha le color al pila, pois incrementa le color e position. Le secunde loop poppa le pila, designa le color poppate como pixel, pois incrementa le position. Como deberea expectar se, isto crea un patron speculare."

#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/tutorial.mdx
msgid "<tt>a9</tt> and <tt>c9</tt> are the processor opcodes for immediate-addressed <tt>LDA</tt> and <tt>CMP</tt> respectively. <tt>01</tt> and <tt>02</tt> are the arguments to these instructions. <tt>d0</tt> is the opcode for <tt>BNE</tt>, and its argument is <tt>02</tt>. This means \"skip over the next two bytes\" (<tt>85 22</tt>, the assembled version of <tt>STA $22</tt>). Try editing the code so <tt>STA</tt> takes a two-byte absolute address rather than a single-byte zero page address (e.g. change <tt>STA $22</tt> to <tt>STA $2222</tt>). Reassemble the code and look at the hexdump again - the argument to <tt>BNE</tt> should now be <tt>03</tt>, because the instruction the processor is skipping past is now three bytes long."
msgstr "<tt>a9</tt> e <tt>c9</tt> es le opcodes del processor pro <tt>LDA</tt> e <tt>CMP</tt> immediate-addressate respectivemente. <tt>01</tt> e <tt>02</tt> es le argumentos a iste instructiones. <tt>d0</tt> es le opcode pro <tt>BNE</tt>, e su argumento es <tt>02</tt>. Iste significa \"saltar super le proxime duo bytes\" (<tt>85 22</tt>, le version assemblate de <tt>STA $22</tt>). Tenta editar le codice assi que <tt>STA</tt> prende un adresse absolute de duo bytes plus tosto que un adresse de pagina zero de sol byte (p.ex. cambiar <tt>STA $22</tt> a <tt>STA $2222</tt>). Reassembla le codice e reguarda le hexdump de novo - le argumento a <tt>BNE</tt> deberea ora esser <tt>03</tt>, proque le instruction que le processor salta super es ora tres bytes longe."

#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/tutorial.mdx
msgid "<tt>checkSnakeCollision</tt> loops through the snake's body segments, checking each byte pair against the head pair. If there is a match, then game over."
msgstr "<tt>checkSnakeCollision</tt> itera per le segmentos del corpore del serpente, verificante cata par de bytes contra le par del capite. Si il ha un coincidentia, pois joco finite."

#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/tutorial.mdx
msgid "<tt>init</tt> and <tt>loop</tt> are both subroutines. <tt>init</tt> initializes the game state, and <tt>loop</tt> is the main game loop."
msgstr "<tt>init</tt> e <tt>loop</tt> es ambe subrutinas. <tt>init</tt> initialisa le stato del joco, e <tt>loop</tt> es le loop principal del joco."

#. TRANSLATORS: Instructions for completing submission on GitHub, including info about large examples
msgid ""
"A GitHub issue has been opened in your browser. Please review and submit it there to complete your contribution. Once approved, your example will be included in the next release.\n"
