#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/tutorial.mdx
msgid "All instructions that support absolute addressing (with the exception of the jump instructions) also have the option to take a single-byte address. This type of addressing is called \"zero page\" - only the first page (the first 256 bytes) of memory is accessible. This is faster, as only one byte needs to be looked up, and takes up less space in the assembled code as well."
msgstr "Tote instructiones que supporta adressage absolute (con le exception del instructiones de salto) tamben ha le option de prender un adresse de un sol byte. Iste typo de adressage es appellate \"pagina zero\" - solo le prime pagina (le prime 256 bytes) de memoria es accessibile. Isto es plus rapide, proque solo un byte debe esser recercate, e occupa minus spatio in le codice assemblate tamben."

