#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/tutorial.mdx
msgid "With absolute addressing, the full memory location is used as the argument to the instruction. For example:"
msgstr "Con adressage absolute, le location de memoria complete es usate como le argumento al instruction. Pro exemplo:"

#. TRANSLATORS: MDX-derived text from packages/learn/tutorial.mdx
msgid "With all these examples you might find it helpful to use the memory monitor in the debugger to watch the memory change. The monitor takes a starting memory location and a number of bytes to display from that location. Both of these are hex values. For example, to display 16 bytes of memory from <tt>$c000</tt>, enter <tt>c000</tt> and <tt>10</tt> into <b>Start</b> and <b>Length</b>, respectively."
msgstr "Con tote iste exemplos tu poterea trovar lo utile usar le monitor de memoria in le debugger pro reguardar le memoria cambiar. Le monitor prende un location de memoria initial e un numero de bytes pro monstrar de ille location. Ambe de iste es valores hex. Pro exemplo, pro monstrar 16 bytes de memoria de <tt>$c000</tt>, entra <tt>c000</tt> e <tt>10</tt> in <b>Start</b> e <b>Longitude</b>, respectivemente."

